#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:1
msgid "Release 1.7 (2014-04-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:3
msgid ""
"In addition to the usual bug fixes, this release has the following new "
"features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:6
msgid ""
"Antiquotation is now allowed inside of quoted attribute names (e.g. `set.\"$"
"{foo}\"`). In the case where the attribute name is just a single "
"antiquotation, the quotes can be dropped (e.g. the above example can be "
"written `set.${foo}`). If an attribute name inside of a set declaration "
"evaluates to `null` (e.g. `{ ${null} = false; }`), then that attribute is "
"not added to the set."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:13
msgid ""
"Experimental support for cryptographically signed binary caches. See [the "
"commit for details](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"0fdf4da0e979f992db75cc17376e455ddc5a96d8)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:17
msgid ""
"An experimental new substituter, `download-via-ssh`, that fetches binaries "
"from remote machines via SSH. Specifying the flags `--option                 "
"use-ssh-substituter true --option ssh-substituter-hosts                 "
"user@hostname` will cause Nix to download binaries from the specified "
"machine, if it has them."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:24
msgid ""
"`nix-store -r` and `nix-build` have a new flag, `--check`, that builds a "
"previously built derivation again, and prints an error message if the output "
"is not exactly the same. This helps to verify whether a derivation is truly "
"deterministic. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:36
msgid ""
"The `nix-instantiate` flags `--eval-only` and `--parse-only` have been "
"renamed to `--eval` and `--parse`, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:39
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` now have a flag `--expr` (or "
"`-E`) that allows you to specify the expression to be evaluated as a command "
"line argument. For instance, `nix-instantiate --eval -E                 '1 + "
"2'` will print `3`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:45
msgid "`nix-shell` improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:47
msgid ""
"It has a new flag, `--packages` (or `-p`), that sets up a build environment "
"containing the specified packages from Nixpkgs. For example, the command"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:53
msgid "will start a shell in which the given packages are present."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:55
msgid ""
"It now uses `shell.nix` as the default expression, falling back to "
"`default.nix` if the former doesn’t exist. This makes it convenient to have "
"a `shell.nix` in your project to set up a nice development environment."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:60
msgid ""
"It evaluates the derivation attribute `shellHook`, if set. Since `stdenv` "
"does not normally execute this hook, it allows you to do `nix-shell`\\-"
"specific setup."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:64
msgid "It preserves the user’s timezone setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:66
msgid ""
"In chroots, Nix now sets up a `/dev` containing only a minimal set of "
"devices (such as `/dev/null`). Note that it only does this if you _don’t_ "
"have `/dev` listed in your `build-chroot-dirs` setting; otherwise, it will "
"bind-mount the `/dev` from outside the chroot."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:71
msgid ""
"Similarly, if you don’t have `/dev/pts` listed in `build-chroot-dirs`, Nix "
"will mount a private `devpts` filesystem on the chroot’s `/dev/pts`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:75
msgid ""
"New built-in function: `builtins.toJSON`, which returns a JSON "
"representation of a value."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:78
msgid ""
"`nix-env -q` has a new flag `--json` to print a JSON representation of the "
"installed or available packages."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:81
msgid ""
"`nix-env` now supports meta attributes with more complex values, such as "
"attribute sets."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:84
msgid "The `-A` flag now allows attribute names with dots in them, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:86
msgid ""
"    $ nix-instantiate --eval '<nixos>' -A 'config.systemd.units."
"\"nscd.service\".text'\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:88
msgid ""
"The `--max-freed` option to `nix-store --gc` now accepts a unit specifier. "
"For example, `nix-store --gc --max-freed                 1G` will free up to "
"1 gigabyte of disk space."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:92
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` has a new flag `--delete-older-than` _N_`d`, which "
"deletes all user environment generations older than _N_ days. Likewise, `nix-"
"env                 --delete-generations` accepts a _N_`d` age limit."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:97
msgid ""
"Nix now heuristically detects whether a build failure was due to a disk-full "
"condition. In that case, the build is not flagged as “permanently failed”. "
"This is mostly useful for Hydra, which needs to distinguish between "
"permanent and transient build failures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:102
msgid ""
"There is a new symbol `__curPos` that expands to an attribute set containing "
"its file name and line and column numbers, e.g. `{ file = \"foo.nix\"; line "
"= 10;                 column = 5; }`. There also is a new builtin function, "
"`unsafeGetAttrPos`, that returns the position of an attribute. This is used "
"by Nixpkgs to provide location information in error messages, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:114
msgid ""
"The garbage collector is now more concurrent with other Nix processes "
"because it releases certain locks earlier."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:117
msgid ""
"The binary tarball installer has been improved. You can now install Nix by "
"running:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:120
msgid ""
"    $ bash <(curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install)\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:122
msgid ""
"More evaluation errors include position information. For instance, selecting "
"a missing attribute will print something like"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:127
msgid "The command `nix-setuid-helper` is gone."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:129
msgid ""
"Nix no longer uses Automake, but instead has a non-recursive, GNU Make-based "
"build system."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:132
msgid ""
"All installed libraries now have the prefix `libnix`. In particular, this "
"gets rid of `libutil`, which could clash with libraries with the same name "
"from other packages."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:136
msgid "Nix now requires a compiler that supports C++11."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:138
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Danny Wilson, Domen Kožar, Eelco "
"Dolstra, Ian-Woo Kim, Ludovic Courtès, Maxim Ivanov, Petr Rockai, Ricardo M. "
"Correia and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""
